Subject: [PATCH] Make the remote server portable across Windows and TLS threads
Base: DoltLite master ffa0eafa93ab695f7863703a2cdaaa3fb7663374 with patches 0001-0010

Use full-width Windows sockets, once-only Winsock startup, and native Windows
locks and worker threads. Keep server TLS connections separate from embedded
client connections, initialize shared Mbed TLS threading, and use stop-aware
nonblocking socket waits on Windows. Preserve upstream pending-connection,
request-body-budget, timeout, and rollback flow.

